# DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash -- 4x DGX Spark GB10, TP=4.
#
# STATE: prepared, not yet bootable. Nothing here has run.
#
#   config.json  architectures ["DeepseekV41ForCausalLM"], model_type deepseek_v41
#
# An earlier version of this comment said the blocker was the image, and that
# was wrong in the direction that matters. An IMAGE is needed only to OVERRIDE
# a file, because an override's contract is the SHA-256 of the file it replaces.
# ADDING files needs no image, and adding is how an architecture arrives:
#
#   vllm.ModelRegistry.register_model(arch, "module:Class")   -- present in the
#     images this fleet runs
#   a .pth at the package root runs before vLLM is imported -- which is exactly
#     what boot_stamps already does (`zz_deneb_boot_stamps.pth`)
#
# So `dsv41_model.py` plus a registering .pth is a composable, image-free path,
# and it is this repo's own mechanism rather than a new idea. What that costs is
# WRITING the model: DeepSeek's reference is ~1,300 lines and a vLLM
# implementation is more of them -- paged KV, graph capture, TP sharding, quant
# loading, the MTP head. Weeks, and unverifiable until it runs.
#
# What still needs an image is the override half: anything that patches vLLM's
# own runtime rather than adding to it -- the sampler, the KV cache coordinator,
# the communicators, the weight loader a pre-sharded backbone would want. And
# one thing is UNKNOWN rather than either: whether V4.1's structural deltas (the
# CED encoder/decoder KV projection, `candidate_topk_blocks`) can be expressed
# against the image's KV cache manager and attention backends without patching
# them. If they cannot, they become overrides and the image is back.
#
# `PROFILE_IMAGE` below therefore names a lineage to build against, not a
# working target.
#
# What IS established, and how (2026-09-10, no GPU involved):
#   - checkpoint 475.2 GiB, 48 shards (`total_size` 510,286,023,000 B)
#   - of that, 189.1 GiB is two Engram lookup tables, isolated in shards 47-48
#   - remainder 286.1 GiB resident -> 71.5 GiB/node at TP=4
#   - the fleet is 4 x ~120 GiB unified LPDDR5X = ~480 GiB, so the stock
#     checkpoint does not fit and ENGRAM_BACKEND=ssd below is not an
#     optimization, it is the precondition for the model existing here at all
PROFILE_DESC="DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash TP=4 (prepared; model/runtime integration incomplete)"

# PLACEHOLDER. This tag serves `deepseek_v4` and will refuse this checkpoint at
# config-load with an unknown-architecture error. It is named here so the
# lineage (venv site-packages, nvcc 13.2, the toolchain the oneshot AR and the
# megakernel already build against) is unambiguous when the real tag arrives.
PROFILE_IMAGE="aidendle94/sparkrun-vllm-ds4-gb10:production-hybrid-1.6"
PROFILE_MODEL_PATH="/home/choiceoh/models/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash"
PROFILE_SERVED_NAME="deepseek-v4.1-flash"
PROFILE_LAUNCHER="start-hy4-tp4.sh"

# Provisional, and it follows PROFILE_IMAGE: the DSV4 lineage installs to the
# venv. If V4.1 arrives on a dist-packages image instead, this line and the
# module set move together -- that is what happened to glm53, whose modules
# cannot mount on a DSV4 image for exactly this reason.
TARGET_PREFIX="/opt/venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/"

# Three of these five are shared, unmodified, with profiles that already serve.
# That is the whole claim this profile makes today -- the model-bound half is
# still missing and is listed under "not yet writable" at the bottom.
#
#   tp_oneshot_ar     3 new files under vllm/distributed/. No model in it.
#   moe_gate_sm121    admits V4.1 with no change, and this was checked rather
#                     than assumed: the fused tier's own guards are
#                     `weight.shape[0] % _GATE_FUSED_BLOCK_N == 0` (BLOCK_N=16)
#                     and `hidden % (_GATE_FUSED_SPLIT_K * _GATE_FUSED_BLOCK_K)
#                     == 0` (1 x 512). V4.1 routes 384 experts over hidden 5120:
#                     384 % 16 = 0, 5120 % 512 = 0. The second, smaller gate the
#                     DSpark block carries (dspark_n_routed_experts 128) clears
#                     the same two: 128 % 16 = 0.
#   sched_decode_first  GLM-5.3's decode-first scheduler, ported unchanged. It
#                     is an AsyncScheduler subclass whose only vllm imports are
#                     AsyncScheduler and SchedulerOutput -- no model, no kernel,
#                     no shape -- so what carries over is the whole thing, not
#                     an analogy. On GLM (39차 DF5) `SCHED_MODE=sequential` held
#                     decoder ITL at 46/49/57 ms, unchanged from decoding alone,
#                     while prefills ran alongside. Nothing is measured here;
#                     the knobs stay at GLM's defaults because inventing new
#                     ones for an unmeasured model would be worse.
#   boot_stamps       phase timings during load. Instrumentation, not a
#                     kernel, and worth more here than on GLM: this model reads
#                     132 GiB/node pre-sharded and 475 without.
#   dsv41_model       new, and the beginning of the architecture rather than
#                     all of it: the per-layer plan, derived from config alone
#                     and held by probes/dsv41_layer_plan.py to predicting the
#                     checkpoint's 96,085 tensor names exactly. Encoder 0..19,
#                     decoder 20..39, KV sourced at [2,8,14,20], indexers at
#                     [2,8,14,20,24,28,32,36], engram at [1,14].
#                     Also carries the explicitly installed reference-model
#                     CED compact indexer for long-context single-token decode.
#                     It does not register a vLLM architecture or activate from
#                     this profile. See dsv41_model/README.md for its scope.
#                     The separate packed-cache adapter covers all eight
#                     reference indexers and drops BF16 key buffers. It also
#                     requires explicit installation; composing this profile
#                     neither activates it nor completes vLLM integration.
#   dsv41_engram      new. The SSD-resident lookup path.
#   dsv41_encoding    new. V4.1's prompt format is not V4's.
#
# glm53_megakernel is NOT here, and the kernel work for it is nonetheless done
# -- see the MK block below for why those are both true.
MODULES="tp_oneshot_ar moe_gate_sm121 sched_decode_first boot_stamps mla_sparse_swa dsv41_vllm dsv41_model dsv41_engram dsv41_encoding"

# --- Engram --------------------------------------------------------------
# Two tables, `layers.{1,14}.engram.embed.weight`, each [384,006,168 x 256]
# F8_E4M3 = 91.55 GiB, plus a [.., 8] F8_E8M0 scale of 2.86 GiB. 189.1 GiB
# together, 39.8% of the checkpoint, and the model card calls them "sparsely
# accessed via token-based lookup" -- which is what makes the demotion possible.
#
# `ssd` keeps the tables in files and reads rows on demand. `device` is the
# stock behaviour and is retained only so a machine that can hold them (nothing
# on this fleet) is expressible; it will OOM here.
ENGRAM_BACKEND=ssd

# Where the shards live. The split is the reference's, not one of ours:
# `ParallelEngramEmbedding` shards by CONTIGUOUS ROW BLOCKS of
# ceil(num_embeddings / world_size), masks the ids outside its block, zeroes
# them and `dist.all_reduce`s. A quarter of the rows per rank, 47.2 GiB/node.
#
# An earlier draft of this file claimed the split followed the 24 disjoint
# prime bucket ranges EngramLayout hands out. It does not, and a checkpoint
# split that way could not be fed to the reference module at all. The
# consequence for I/O is that a rank's per-token read count is Binomial(24,
# 1/4) -- mean 6, sd 2.1 -- rather than a fixed 6; at batch 32 over two tables
# that is mean 384, sd 17, so the measured step stands but no per-token bound
# exists. probes/dsv41_engram_diff.py holds this arithmetic to being
# bit-identical to the reference over all four ranks.
#
# This is necessary for srv1 but NOT sufficient, and saying otherwise was an
# error in an earlier draft of this file. The launcher bind-mounts the
# checkpoint per node and every rank reads all of it (GLM-5.3's boot log reads
# 184.2 GiB on each worker), so a node needs 475 GiB rather than its quarter.
# srv1 has 153 GiB free and its 498 GB of /home is the RUNNING GLM-5.3's
# checkpoint (185 GB) and fp8 cache (216 GB) -- not freeable without taking
# production down. Splitting engram removes 47.3 GiB of a 322 GiB shortfall.
#
# Per-rank pre-sharding of the backbone closes the rest: 71.5 + 47.3 = 118.8
# GiB per node fits srv1 with 34 GiB spare, leaves GLM-5.3 in place so an A/B
# is possible, and cuts the boot read from 475 to 119 GiB/node (61 s -> 15 s at
# the 7.76 GiB/s GLM measures). It needs a builder and a pre-sharded loader,
# listed under "not yet writable" below.
ENGRAM_SHARD_DIR="/home/choiceoh/models/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-engram"

# Reads per token, derived from config rather than guessed:
#   engram_max_ngram_size 4 -> 3 n-gram sizes (2/3/4-gram)
#   engram_n_heads 8, engram_layer_ids [1, 14]
#   3 x 8 x 2 = 48 rows/token, 12 after the TP split
# A batch-32 decode step asks a rank for 384 random reads. srv4's NVMe
# (ESL04TBTLCZ, 4 TB) measured 157,357 IOPS at QD32 O_DIRECT, and the step's
# own strided path reaches 88,790 -- 56% of the drive, so the drive is not the
# constraint. The ISSUE PATH is: demand paging through mmap costs one fault per
# row, serialized, 384 x 62 us = 24 ms against a ~20 ms step, and dispatching
# one pool task per read instead of one per thread measured 52,607 IOPS against
# 88,790 for the same reads on the same drive.
#
# None of that is what the step pays, because the reads do not block. Issued at
# layer 0 and collected at the layer, the residual stall is 0.07 ms p95 at
# layer 14 and 0.09 ms p95 for both tables once layer 1 is drafted a step
# early: 0.5% of the step. probes/dsv41_engram_probe.py, 150 steps.
ENGRAM_QUEUE_DEPTH=32

# Prefetch distance in layers. The addresses do not depend on any hidden state
# -- the reference `NgramHashState.forward(input_ids, start_pos)` takes token
# ids and nothing else -- so all 48 hashes for a step are known before layer 0
# runs and the reads can be issued that early. Layer 14 has 13 layers of
# compute to hide behind and clears it. Layer 1 has one layer and does not:
# 4.19 ms p95 is left unhidden, so its rows want fetching during the PREVIOUS
# step, off the DSpark draft block (dspark_block_size 5) whose ids already
# determine the hashes. Measured that way both tables cost 0.09 ms p95, and the
# price is 26% of layer-1 reads discarded at 75% acceptance -- waste the IOPS
# budget absorbs. Set to 0 to issue at the layer itself and eat the stall; that
# is the measurement baseline, not a serving setting.
ENGRAM_PREFETCH_LAYERS=14

# --- megakernel (geometry prepared; V4.1 seam experimental, NOT mounted) ---
# The core is absent from MODULES above on purpose. Mounting it takes a second
# module carrying `_deneb_mk_hook()` -- glm53 gets that from glm53_kernels,
# dsv4 from dsv4_mhc_tilelang -- and both are OVERRIDES of
# vllm/model_executor/kernels/mhc/tilelang.py, so a V4.1 one needs a preimage
# SHA-256 from an image that does not exist. tests/test_logic.py enforces the
# pairing across every profile, on the grounds that a core without a hook logs
# `armed` and routes nothing. It is right, and the core stays out until
# dsv41_mhc can be written.
#
# The KERNEL change is done and verified regardless, because it is the part
# that did not need an image:
#   - `HIDDEN` is now a template parameter, defaulting to 4096, with a second
#     instantiation at HIDDEN_V41 = 5120
#   - probes/mk_mhc_hidden_compile.py compiles all eight entry points for
#     sm_121a: 158 registers (128 for the bf16 AR variant), ZERO spills, and
#     the counts are IDENTICAL at 4096 and 5120 -- the MHC_EPT 16 -> 20 growth
#     cost nothing, so occupancy and therefore the persistent grid are
#     unchanged
#   - the same probe run against the pre-change source reports the same
#     158/128/158/158, which is the receipt that GLM-5.3 and V4-Flash are
#     untouched by this
#   - probes/mk_mhc_numeric.py RUNS it, on this fleet's GPU, at both hidden
#     sizes and T in {1,7,24,32,33,64,127,128}. Inputs are chosen so the answer
#     is analytic (identity comb_mix, unit post_mix -> residual_out[t,j,h] is
#     j+2 everywhere), so the check is exact on every one of T x HC x HID
#     elements rather than an average that could drift. It also pins the RMS
#     the tail takes, NCHUNK * 13824 / (4 * HID) = 13.5, which is equal at both
#     sizes ONLY because NCHUNK tracked HID.
#     Mutating NCHUNK back to HIDDEN/HCHUNK leaves 4096 passing and fails 5120
#     on all three checks -- the probe was verified to detect the regression it
#     exists for, not merely to pass.
#     Still not established: the sinkhorn and projection arithmetic, which this
#     deliberately zeroes out to avoid grading the kernel against a hand-ported
#     reference. That is the extension's own self-test, and it needs an image.
#   - the segment's token bound is now its own constant. MAX_TOK was doing
#     three jobs -- this workspace, the SMLP lane's admission gate
#     (`T > MAX_TOK -> return None`) and the MLA workspace cap -- so its value
#     of 32 was chosen for a different lane and left mHC able to serve only
#     C <= 5 at six tokens per sequence. Above that it fell back to the stock
#     post+big_fuse pair: not slower, ARMED AND NOT RUNNING. MHC_MAX_TOK
#     (`-D MHC_MAX_TOK_DEF`, default 128) lifts that; MAX_TOK stays 32 so
#     nothing the SMLP or MLA lanes do moves. Workspace 0.30 -> 1.51 MiB,
#     registers unchanged at 158/128, because the constant appears only in
#     pointer strides and one device counter.
#     This lifts the KERNEL's gate. The WRAPPER the hook sits in has its own
#     (DSV4's is inside `use_small_fma`, T <= 16) and that one is dsv41_mhc's
#     to place.
# Geometry support alone does not implement the V4.1 MHC seam. The reference
# consumes the PREVIOUS sublayer's pre mix, returns the newly computed pre mix,
# and rounds post/pre to BF16 BEFORE the projection/RMS statistics. Its norm
# epsilon is 1e-20, separate from hc_eps=1e-6. The legacy fused contract differs
# on each point. `_mhc_v41_call` / `run_mhc_v41` implement the distinct seam;
# probes/mk_mhc_geometry_bench.py checks it separately with nonzero projections,
# all output coefficients and changed-input graph replay. GPU correctness and
# model call-site ownership must pass before this profile mounts or arms it.
#
# MK_SEG_MHC is reachable and the other three are not, for the same reasons
# they are unreachable on DSV4 (see dsv4.env), re-checked against V4.1's config:
#   MK_SEG_KDA   no linear-attention layer exists in this model
#   MK_SEG_MLA   this model has rope 64, index_topk 512, a compressor, a
#                sliding window, and now cross-layer KV sourcing
#                (kv_source_layer_ids [2,8,14,20]) -- GLM's kernel is
#                NoPE/topk-2048
#   MK_SEG_GEMM  the lane is W4 (e2m1 packs); V4.1's dense weights are
#                block-fp8 (weight_block_size [32,32], scale_fmt ue8m0)
#
# MHC geometry is reachable because it is one the kernel already
# compiles for. V4.1's hc_mult 4, hc_sinkhorn_iters 20 and hc_eps 1e-6 are
# GLM-5.3's and V4-Flash's values exactly, so HC=4, NOUT=HC*(2+HC)=24 and
# SINKHORN_SERVED=20 all carry. ONE constant did not: hidden is 5120 here and
# the kernel had `constexpr int HIDDEN = 4096` with `_mk_mhc_eligible` pinning
# it. Generalizing that constant is this profile's kernel change; 5120 divides
# both HCHUNK (256 -> NCHUNK 20) and MK_THREADS (256 -> MHC_EPT 20), so the
# decomposition stays integral and no tail case appears.
#
# NOTHING is measured. The MK pair is a reduce-order change (rel 1e-3 class),
# not bit-exact, and the ladder that dsv4.env spells out applies here with one
# addition -- the register file. MHC_EPT 16 -> 20 grows res[HC][MHC_EPT],
# nw[] and vals[] by a quarter, so `-Xptxas -v` and an occupancy check come
# before any numerics run, and both come before arming.
VLLM_GLM53_MEGAKERNEL=0
VLLM_GLM53_MK_MHC=0
VLLM_GLM53_MK_PDL=0

# --- serving -------------------------------------------------------------
# GPU_MEM is deliberately NOT pinned to dsv4's 0.60. The arithmetic that
# decides it is different here and worth writing down, because it is the one
# place V4.1 is CHEAPER than what runs today:
#
#   GLM-5.3 today   50.0 GiB weights + ~27 GiB KV inside a 76.9 GiB budget
#                   (gpu_memory_utilization 0.6429 of 119.7 GiB), holding
#                   1056 blocks x 2304 = 2,433,024 tokens at fp8_e4m3
#   V4.1 here       71.5 GiB weights, +21.5 GiB, leaving ~5.4 GiB at the same
#                   budget -- but a token costs far less. CED projects the
#                   decoder's global KV from the final encoder states, so only
#                   kv_source_layer_ids [2,8,14,20] carry it: 4 layers x
#                   head_dim 512 x num_key_value_heads 1 at FP4 is ~1 KiB/token
#                   against GLM's measured ~11 KiB, and the card's "SWA Bounded
#                   Replay ... roughly 1/8" says the same thing from the other
#                   side.
#
# If that holds, 5.4 GiB buys MORE context than GLM's 27 GiB does and the
# budget never needs raising. It is an ESTIMATE derived from config, it is the
# single number this whole comparison rests on, and it is the first thing to
# measure when an image exists -- which is why the value is left unset here
# rather than pinned to a number nobody has confirmed.
GMU_NOTE="unset on purpose -- KV bytes/token is estimated, not measured; see block above"

# The ported scheduler, off by default. Turning it on is a serving change and
# this profile has never booted; DECODE_FIRST=1 with SCHED_MODE=sequential is
# what GLM serves, and is where to start once there is something to measure.
# start-hy4-tp4.sh learned the knob in 41차; it had none, so the port was a
# launcher change as much as a module one.
DECODE_FIRST=0

# The scheduler's knobs, at GLM-5.3's 39차 values. They are declared rather
# than left to the module's defaults for two reasons: the launcher forwards a
# profile's VLLM_* keys automatically, so an undeclared knob cannot be set at
# all here; and writing them down is what makes it visible that they are
# GLM's numbers on a model nobody has measured.
#
# `sequential` was GLM's answer to a specific finding -- mixing prefill into a
# decode step costs a fixed ~0.4 s on that stack, so running the two in turns
# beat interleaving them for BOTH. Whether V4.1 shares that shape is unknown:
# it has a different step composition, a CED encoder/decoder split and three
# MTP layers. Re-measure before believing any of these.
VLLM_GLM53_SCHED_MODE=sequential
VLLM_GLM53_SCHED_MAX_WAIT_S=20
VLLM_GLM53_SCHED_DECODE_STEPS=6
VLLM_GLM53_SCHED_MIXED_CHUNK=1152
VLLM_GLM53_SCHED_PREFILL_FLOOR=1000

# 1M, as the checkpoint declares (max_position_embeddings 1048576 with yarn
# factor 16 over an original 65536).
MAX_LEN=1048576

# Multimodal is native here rather than grafted: the checkpoint carries a
# DeepSeek-ViT tower (vision_config, 32 layers, 0.8 GiB) and an image_token_id
# in the top-level config. Text-only until the tower is exercised once --
# GLM-5.3's vision bring-up cost a 13-minute production outage to a NameError
# in an overlay, and that was on a model already serving.
MM_LIMIT='{"image":0,"video":0}'

# DSpark, as on DSV4 -- no draft model file, the block is in the checkpoint.
# It is a bigger block here: num_nextn_predict_layers 3 (V4 had 1) with its own
# 128-expert MoE and dspark_markov_rank 256.
SPEC_METHOD=dspark

# The routed experts are MXFP4 (`expert_dtype: fp4` in quantization_config),
# and vllm/models/deepseek_v4/quant_config.py only reaches for the config that
# knows that when `model_type == "deepseek_v4"` OR the user names it. V4.1's
# model_type is `deepseek_v41`, so without this the experts are classified FP8,
# every fp4 backend answers "not supported for FP8 MoE", and the model runs --
# wrongly -- on an fp8 lane. Naming it is the supported escape hatch and needs
# no image change.
QUANT=deepseek_v4_fp8

# --- boot ladder, measured 2026-09-11 on the ds4 image ------------------
# aidendle94/sparkrun-vllm-ds4-gb10:production-hybrid-1.6, GLM-5.3 stopped,
# `--load-format dummy`, 2 layers, 8 experts, TP1. Each rung is a real error
# that was fixed, not a step that was skipped:
#
#   1. transformers does not know `deepseek_v41`  -> dsv41_config registers the
#      config type through AutoConfig. Before this, ModelConfig failed with a
#      message about the checkpoint being unrecognized.
#   2. architecture unsupported                    -> dsv41_arch registers
#      DeepseekV41ForCausalLM. No image rebuild: adding an architecture needs
#      no preimage.
#   3. hidden_size 768                             -> the outer config is a
#      FLAT VIEW of text_config. The V4 model reads hf_config directly, and a
#      nested config answers with PretrainedConfig defaults without complaint.
#   4. num_hash_layers AttributeError              -> 0 on the config class.
#      V4 hashed its first layers; V4.1 has engram instead.
#   5. kv-cache dtype                              -> --kv-cache-dtype fp8_e4m3.
#      DeepseekV4's fp8_ds_mla layout takes nothing else.
#   6. host OOM at 384 experts                     -> a test-size knob, not a
#      finding.
#
# It then CONSTRUCTS the whole model, and after three more rungs it SERVES:
#
#   7. o-projection                                -> the image's fused fp8
#      einsum wants a 3-D weight, which vLLM only builds on the DeepGEMM
#      block-scaled kernel, which is only selected at [128,128]. At [32,32]
#      the Triton kernel is selected, wo_a stays 2-D, and the einsum asserts
#      t.dim() == N. dsv41_o_proj dequantizes wo_a to bf16 and does the
#      grouped einsum -- which is what DeepSeek's own reference does, and its
#      comment says so ("convert.py dequantizes it to bf16; an fp8 grouped
#      GEMM would halve the memory"). +1.3 GiB/rank across 40 layers.
#      Reshaping to 3-D instead would silence the assertion and read 32-wide
#      scales as 128-wide: finite, plausible, wrong.
#   8. MoE lane                                  -> the first answer here was
#      WRONG and is kept because the way it was wrong is the point.
#      deep_gemm_mega_moe refused V4.1 in symmetric-buffer sizing, and
#      sweeping it isolated the rule exactly: the L1 activation SCALE slice is
#      `(intermediate / 128) * 4` bytes and must be 16-aligned, so
#      `intermediate % 512 == 0`; V4.1 ships 2304 = 4.5 x 512 and V4 ships
#      2048. Padding the intermediate to 2560 does clear it -- zero-padded
#      SwiGLU lanes contribute exactly zero, verified bit-identical -- and it
#      was implemented and then DELETED, because clearing that assertion only
#      exposes the next line:
#
#          NotImplementedError: DeepGEMM MegaMoE requires SM100 GPUs.
#
#      GB10 is SM121. mega_moe was never available to this fleet, for V4 or
#      V4.1, at any intermediate size. A precisely measured constraint on a
#      path that cannot run is still a wasted afternoon, and the lesson is to
#      ask what the hardware supports before optimizing what the kernel wants.
#
#      The real lane is B12X MXFP4, and what unlocks it is a QUANT CONFIG, not
#      a backend flag. vllm/models/deepseek_v4/quant_config.py:
#
#          if model_type == "deepseek_v4" or user_quant == "deepseek_v4_fp8":
#              return "deepseek_v4_fp8"
#          return None
#
#      V4.1's model_type is `deepseek_v41`, so it fell through to the stock
#      Fp8Config, the routed experts were classified FP8 rather than the fp4
#      they are, and every fp4 backend answered "not supported for FP8 MoE".
#      The `user_quant` arm is the supported escape hatch and needs no image
#      change: `--quantization deepseek_v4_fp8`. With it:
#
#          DeepSeek V4 expert_dtype resolved to 'fp4'
#          Using 'B12X' Mxfp4 MoE backend.
#
#  10. E8M0 scales                               -> [32,32] also sends the
#      DENSE linears to Triton, which cannot even NAME the dtype
#      (`KeyError: 'float8_e8m0fnu'`). dsv41_scales casts those scales to
#      float32 after loading -- lossless, since E8M0 is a bare exponent and
#      all 256 codes round-trip identically (probes/dsv41_scales.py walks the
#      whole domain). Scoped to dense linears only: MXFP4 WANTS e8m0 expert
#      scales, and converting those would break the lane step 8 just opened.
#   9. compress_ratio 2                            -> vLLM's sparse_swa
#      enumerated V4's ratios (1, 4, 128) and raised otherwise. V4.1
#      compresses EVERY layer at 2. mla_sparse_swa (which this fleet already
#      overrides, preimage 6a8df7ab..., verified against this image) now
#      derives the key for any ratio and reproduces V4's three names exactly.
#      That module is therefore in MODULES for dsv41.
#
# BOOTED AND GENERATED, 2026-09-11:
#
#   Resolved architecture: DeepseekV41ForCausalLM
#   Selected TritonFp8BlockScaledMMKernel for Fp8LinearMethod
#   Using DeepSeek's fp8_ds_mla KV cache format.
#   DeepSeek V4 expert_dtype resolved to 'fp4'
#   Using 'B12X' Mxfp4 MoE backend.
#   [dsv41_scales] wrapped 9 dense-linear quant method(s)
#   [dsv41_scales] first conversion: 1 E8M0 scale(s) -> fp32
#   Application startup complete.
#   POST /v1/completions -> 8 tokens
#
# The tokens are gibberish because --load-format dummy fills the weights with
# noise. What the run establishes is the PIPELINE: tokenizer, embedding,
# compressor, indexer, sparse SWA attention, the bf16 o-projection, the MoE,
# the head and the sampler all execute on V4.1's shapes. It does not
# establish a single thing about quality, and must never be cited as if it
# did.
#
# Not yet: real weights (needs load_weights against the pre-shard), TP=4,
# engram, DSpark's 3 stages, vision, and every performance question.
#
# --- remaining runtime integration --------------------------------------
# New model files can be added without a preimage. Overrides of existing
# runtime files still need a verified image preimage. The reference-only
# component implementations below do not complete vLLM serving integration.
#
#   dsv41_attention   head_dim 512 / qk_rope_head_dim 64 / q_lora_rank 1280 /
#                     o_lora_rank 1024 / o_groups 8, and the CED split (20-layer
#                     causal encoder, 20-layer decoder) that changes where KV
#                     comes from
#   dsv41_indexer     index_n_heads 32 (V4: 64), index_head_dim 128,
#                     index_topk 512, and index_source_layer_ids -- eight
#                     sourcing layers plus candidate_source_layer_id 20 with
#                     candidate_topk_blocks 2048 at candidate_block_size 8
#                     Reference-only compact scoring is implemented in
#                     dsv41_model; GPU proof and paged serving remain pending.
#   dsv41_model       engram call sites, Single-Pass mHC, SWA Bounded Replay,
#                     the 3-layer DSpark head
#   dsv41_mhc         the `_deneb_mk_hook()` half of MK_SEG_MHC. dsv4 and glm53
#                     need it as an OVERRIDE of
#                     vllm/model_executor/kernels/mhc/tilelang.py because their
#                     model code is the image's. Ours would not be: a model we
#                     write carries its own hook, so this stops being an
#                     override the moment dsv41_model exists. The kernel it
#                     hooks needs the V4.1 numerical-contract and ownership
#                     gates above; HIDDEN_V41 geometry alone is insufficient.
#                     See
#                     the note above on how little the segment is worth (3.3%
#                     of an armed GLM decode step, and V4.1 ships its own
#                     single-pass mHC)
#   dsv41_model       (partly written; see MODULES) the rest of the
#                     architecture plus the .pth that registers it. NEW files,
#                     so no image -- this is the work, not a blocker. Done:
#                     engram end to end, and the CED layer plan. Unwritten: the
#                     attention itself, the indexer's candidate blocks
#                     (candidate_topk_blocks 2048 at block size 8), the
#                     3-layer DSpark head, the ViT, and load_weights.
#   dsv41_preshard    BUILT AND MEASURED on the real checkpoint, 2026-09-10.
#                     Rank 0 of 4: `build` wrote 26,961 tensors / 84.7 GiB in
#                     2m29s, `verify` read it back -- layout from
#                     __metadata__, the whole name set against the source
#                     index, and 252 tensors / 2.66 GiB byte-for-byte -- and
#                     tools/dsv41_engram_shard.py added both engram tables,
#                     45.8 GiB, verified against the source. 133 GiB on disk
#                     against the 131.9 GiB predicted.
#                     Rank 1 followed (2m26s, 84.7 GiB, 973 tensors / 6.07
#                     GiB byte-exact) and the two REAL files share no expert
#                     tensor: rank 0 holds ids [0, 95] and rank 1 [96, 191],
#                     contiguous blocks, as expert_rank says.
#                     The loader half (dsv41_model/dsv41_preshard_load.py)
#                     reads both files' headers and its expected name set
#                     matches each exactly; it refuses another rank's file,
#                     another world size, another --mtp mode, and a file with
#                     no __metadata__.
#                     Still unwritten: the model-side load_weights that
#                     consumes it, because there is no model yet.
#                     The capacity question it answers was already answered:
#                     tools/dsv41_preshard.py `plan` reads all 48 shard headers
#                     and reports 131.9 GiB per rank against today's 475.2 --
#                     67.2 experts (96 of 384 per layer, expert-parallel),
#                     47.2 engram (a quarter of the rows), 17.5 replicated.
#                     srv1's 153 GiB free clears that by 21 GiB, where today it
#                     is short by 322. `--mtp ep` would take it to 126.9 and
#                     `--dense tp` to 121.4; neither is needed.
#                     Pre-sharding is also the only path that leaves GLM-5.3
#                     serving while this is brought up, and it cuts the boot
#                     read from 475 to 132 GiB/node.
#                     OPEN: that 21 GiB has to also hold whatever compile cache
#                     this model wants. GLM-5.3's fp8 cache on srv1 is 216 GB.
#                     V4.1 ships fp8 weights so it may need nothing comparable,
#                     but nothing has established that.
#   dsv41_tokenizer   engram_compressed_vocab_size 99092 must equal what
#                     `build_compressed_token_map` derives from the shipped
#                     tokenizer, and the reference asserts it -- a mismatch
#                     silently rehashes both tables
